## What This Means for M64's Architecture

The expanded analyte list reinforces that the **general discordance heuristic** (Tier B detection) isn't optional — it's essential. Many of these patterns share the same structural logic despite involving completely different biochemistry. M64 needs to be able to ask "is there a serum-function disconnect here?" even for analytes where nobody has formally characterized the discordance pattern yet.

I'd recommend updating the spec to formalize the two-layer detection architecture: Layer 1 (signature-matched, high confidence) and Layer 2 (general heuristic, exploratory confidence), with clear governance differences in how each layer's outputs are surfaced and how the B2C vs B2MD payloads differ for exploratory-confidence flags.

